From: cjom <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: reset the argument vector on every game load

parse_command_params() only ever appends: it copies each token into
cmd_params[cmd_params_num] and increments, and never rewinds. The only
resets are init_command_params(), called from retro_init() -- once per
process -- and from retro_reset().

retro_load_game() never resets it. That is invisible to a frontend which
unloads and reloads the shared object for each game, but a frontend that
keeps the core loaded and simply calls retro_load_game() again hands
ScummVM's main() the previous game's arguments as well as the new ones:

  User picked target 'manhole' (engine ID 'made', game ID 'manhole')...
  scummvm: Stray argument 'made:manhole'
  Usage: scummvm [OPTIONS]... [GAME]

ScummVM accepts at most one game argument, so it prints usage and refuses
to start. The first game of a session runs, every one after it fails --
and because the failure is a clean exit rather than a crash, the frontend
just drops back to its own UI with nothing logged on its side.

The argument vector describes exactly one game, so building it belongs in
retro_load_game(). Reset it there, before the LIBRETRO_DEBUG block that
may itself append to it.

diff --git a/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp b/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
index 2a59b2a..e3bb35a 100644
--- a/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
+++ b/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
@@ -983,6 +983,22 @@ bool retro_load_game(const struct retro_game_info *game) {
 		return false;
 	}
 
+	/* Reset the argument vector for this game. parse_command_params() only ever
+	   appends -- it increments cmd_params_num and never rewinds it -- and until
+	   now the only resets were retro_init() (once per process) and
+	   retro_reset(). A frontend that keeps the core loaded between games, rather
+	   than unloading the library each time, therefore handed ScummVM's main()
+	   the previous game's arguments as well as the new ones, and it refused to
+	   start:
+
+	     User picked target 'manhole' (engine ID 'made', game ID 'manhole')...
+	     scummvm: Stray argument 'made:manhole'
+	     Usage: scummvm [OPTIONS]... [GAME]
+
+	   so the first launch worked and every launch after it died. The argument
+	   vector describes one game, so building it belongs here. */
+	init_command_params();
+
 #ifdef LIBRETRO_DEBUG
 	char debug_buf [20];
 	sprintf(debug_buf, "--debuglevel=11");
